=== parameters ===
reuse 200x750; true factor + nuisance raw_factor2
MU_STRONG=0.0025 (inflated teaching) MU_WEAK=0.001 (realistic-weak foil)
look-ahead: shift(1) weights; lagged impact vol; neutralize uses log_mcap.shift(1)
cost model: P2 10 bps one-way + √impact
overlapping IC windows inflate IC autocorr / ICIR SE (not mean IC) — use non-overlap or NW

=== neutralization before / after (strong; lagged mcap) ===
true_factor RankIC mean before_neut=0.0761 after=0.1119
nuisance_factor RankIC mean after_neut=-0.0027 (should be ~0)
recovery corr after_neut=0.9663
neutralize covariates: industry (static) + log_mcap.shift(1) only — no same-day mcap

=== strong vs weak (side-by-side portfolio metrics) ===
strong MU=0.0025 RankIC=0.1119 ICIR=4.636 gross_SR=4.495 net_SR=3.668 turn=1.0586
weak   MU=0.0010 RankIC=0.0431 ICIR=1.769 gross_SR=1.619 net_SR=0.792 turn=1.0586
teach: weak RankIC is the live-like case; costs often erase net edge — multi-factor combination exists to stack weak signals

=== single vs equal-weight multi-factor (strong) ===
true_only                gross_SR=4.495 net_SR=3.668 turn=1.0586 NAV=32.403 IC=0.1119
nuisance_only            gross_SR=-1.429 net_SR=-8.500 turn=1.3895 NAV=0.273 IC=-0.0027
ew_true_plus_nuisance    gross_SR=4.497 net_SR=3.085 turn=1.3009 NAV=8.293 IC=0.0788
teach: blending a null nuisance dilutes IC/net SR — combining ≠ free lunch; combine *informed* weak factors

=== multi-factor honesty on WEAK panel ===
weak_true_only               gross_SR=1.619 net_SR=0.792 turn=1.0586 IC=0.0431
weak_ew_true_plus_nuisance   gross_SR=1.637 net_SR=0.225 turn=1.3009 IC=0.0306

=== turnover–cost table (strong true factor) ===
hold= 1d mean_turn=1.0586 net_SR=3.668 NAV=32.403
hold= 5d mean_turn=0.2107 net_SR=4.289 NAV=59.940
hold=10d mean_turn=0.1035 net_SR=4.360 NAV=63.125
hold=20d mean_turn=0.0533 net_SR=4.230 NAV=53.796

=== turnover–cost table (WEAK true factor) ===
hold= 1d mean_turn=1.0586 net_SR=0.792 NAV=1.863
hold= 5d mean_turn=0.2107 net_SR=1.422 NAV=3.483
hold=10d mean_turn=0.1035 net_SR=1.501 NAV=3.748
hold=20d mean_turn=0.0533 net_SR=1.392 NAV=3.333
teach: on weak signals, cutting turnover is often the difference between net>0 and net≈0

